= Scientific literature — Technical =

Scientific literature can be modeled as a versioned, citation-linked corpus of research objects with heterogeneous publication states. Interpretation depends on genre, review status, version, provenance, methods, evidence, corrections, and the relation between individual claims and the broader evidence base.

== Modeling / implementation cautions ==
* scientific literature ≠ all scientific knowledge
* publication ≠ correctness
* one paper ≠ scientific consensus

== References ==
* National Academies of Sciences, Engineering, and Medicine, reports on communicating and evaluating scientific research.
* UNESCO, ''Recommendation on Open Science'' (2021), scientific publications and knowledge communication.
